      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Abhishek!\n\nThe method signature is:\n\n```\nvoid selectPresentation(int presentationId, int programId);\n```\n\nThe first argument is presentation ID, the second is program ID.\n\nHere we set the first argument to `-2` and say that we use presentation ID `-2`, thus consistent:\n\n```\n        // Negative presentation IDs are not allowed, but \u0027-1\u0027 is OK, so use \u0027-2\u0027.\n        ASSERT_STATUS(EX_ILLEGAL_ARGUMENT, stream.get()-\u003eselectPresentation(-2, 0));\n```\n\nSame for \"program ID\" value used in the second argument. Program IDs can be negative, but must be within 16-bit range. The test provides values that are beyond this range and expects argument rejection.\n\nCould you please clarify where exactly are you seeing a contradiction?",
