      "message": "Ah, indeed that expression is not what I intended. I was thinking of values below the minimum of `int16_t`.\n\nSo the correct expression should be:\n\n`static_cast\u003cint32_t\u003e(std::numeric_limits\u003cint16_t\u003e::min()) - 1)` (`int16_t` instead of `uint16_t`).\n\nI\u0027m leaving `uint16_t` for over the max calculation because maybe the HAL uses unsigned 16-bits underneath. The standard doesn\u0027t say \"signed 16-bit values\" explicitly.\n\n---\n\nNote that `-2` for `programID` is a correct value, at least by the standard. See Dean\u0027s comment here: https://b.corp.google.com/issues/466889574#comment3.",
